  "id": "Compound::DB00998 - Gene::3350",
  "verbalization": "Frovatriptan, a serotonin 1b/d receptor agonist, is linked to Htr1a through a shared pathway involving organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds and serotonin agonists. The evidence suggests that Frovatriptan, along with Rizatriptan and Zolmitriptan, belongs to a class of compounds that bind to Htr1a. This relationship is supported by the presence of a common ancestor in the serotonin agonist category, indicating a functional link between these drugs and the receptor. The integration of multiple paths highlights a consistent mechanism where serotonin receptor agonists, through a shared biological pathway, interact with Htr1a. The evidence does not provide direct binding evidence between Frovatriptan and Htr1a, but the shared classification and the presence of a common ancestor suggest a functional or pharmacological relationship that warrants further investigation.",
